WEBVTT

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:22.580
Beware.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.310
Ring for escape.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.200
There's anything particularly scary about Wolf Creek.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.550
What about that place?

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.040
That's the Marling's house. You want to stay away from that couple?

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.780
The woods aren't really safe after dark.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.530
Why? Is that when the monsters come out or something?

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.460
When the sun rises, the werewolf sheds its skin.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.870
And if someone finds its skin and destroys it before the next full moon is at its highest point,

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.650
the curse is over, and the werewolf inside the person dies.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.990
What were you doing out in the woods?

00:00:59.170 --> 00:00:59.970
Just hate these a-

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.780
And what did we say about the Marlings?

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:07.000
take it easy what is going on in here ask your nephew he's the one holding the ibex it was the

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.140
marlings what about them they came over for a little visit last night and guess what wolves

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:28.750
that's ridiculous oh yeah and how do you explain this well

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.800
It must have been a bear or something, a rabbit fox.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.020
A rabbit fox? It wasn't a fox.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.880
I saw it. It was part animal, part human.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.080
It had fangs and claws and pointy ears.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.200
Sorry, but that's a werewolf.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.760
Hannah said the woods weren't safe, and now I know why.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.160
Oh, you've been talking to Hannah.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:57.440
Alex, Hannah's older brother was bitten by a wolf

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.810
a year ago, right out behind the marlings.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.730
The wolf was never caught, but Hannah has spent days out there trying to find it.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.150
Yeah, that's why we locked you in.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.450
We couldn't risk having you wandering around in the woods.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.830
Or bothering the marlings.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.420
Oh, right. Let's be polite to the werewolves next door.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.860
Marlings are werewolves?

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:19.730
Are you sure?

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:20.570
I should be.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.310
They were trying to get in my window.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.010
That's weird.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:25.650
Werewolves don't usually climb.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.730
Oh, yeah. And how many werewolves have you seen?

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:28.570
Lots of them.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:29.390
Excuse me?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.210
the woods. That's what I've been trying to warn you about. I didn't tell you at first because I was

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:40.200
afraid you wouldn't believe me. That's why my brother ran away. He tried to tell people what he

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:49.870
saw. They wouldn't listen. Nobody believed him. Hannah, I believe you. I guess I've always been

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:55.040
around. They used to be able to hide in the woods. You know, get food and stuff. Except now with all

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.340
the trees being chopped down and the city's taking up so much space. There's no room for them.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.210
They've got to go someplace.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.460
That must be what my aunt was talking about.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.220
She said they were working on some kind of secret project.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.020
They must be taking pictures of werewolves through the government.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.060
You know, some kind of bizarro X-Files thing.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.400
So what are you going to do now?

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.960
Well, first, I'm going to forget about the Chiller Magazine contest.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.180
Good idea.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.460
This is too good for them.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.720
I'm going big time.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:21.620
Newsweek.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.340
No, people.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.760
No, even better, the Chiller Exposer.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:27.900
No!

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.470
What happened to you last night?

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.020
We waited for an hour out there.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.660
Arjun almost got eaten alive by mosquitoes.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.180
Yeah.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.140
They like my blood.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.600
I didn't have to go to the woods to see any werewolves.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.480
They came to me.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:40.960
What?

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.760
Uh-huh. Right up to my house.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.130
Yeah, right.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:44.630
Sure.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:45.620
Right.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.080
Okay, I'll prove it to you.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.320
Tonight, meet me at the Marling house.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:50.080
Midnight.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.000
That is, if you're not chicken.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.040
clock.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:53.950
Good luck.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:54.690
clock.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.570
calling National Exposer.

